{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch","id":943078,"title":"The visage of an Exarch...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-03T16:05:58-07:00","id":943078,"title":"The visage of an Exarch...","content":"Suppose a player played a Seer of the Throne through an epic campaign, to archmastery, culminating in becoming a Minister. They meet an Exarch for the first time, and see...?<br /> <br /> I've been re-reading <i>Imperial Mysteries</i> and the sample Exarch Ochema was maddeningly vague in its writeup. But an Exarch...? Sure, I know, merely seeing one would be sanity-blasting even to a Minister...but...what <i>would</i> these Ministers see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:37:42-07:00","id":943095,"title":"","content":"Well they are whole and complete supernal platonic god symbols in the center of the supernal realms fused to their domains. The exarch would appear however the Archmasters &quot;lustrum&quot; symbolizes them. (They don't have a &quot;Real&quot; shape they have to be recognized as allegory)<br /> <br /> Specifically The exarchs are anthropomorphized perfect symbols of tyranny and oppression mixed with transhuman/alien intelligence. Panopticon might appear as a woman vaguely resembling a lover you knew who knows you every secret or an unending fractal of eyeballs or both. speaking to them in any case is probably impossible They are the reason for certain concepts existing in the world of darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4641-pebbles","name":"Pebbles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:41:28-07:00","id":943097,"title":"","content":"That was the gist I seemed to get from the text, but...how would I represent that? Are Exarchs of mutable appearance? Would the Raptor literally appear differently to everyone viewing it? How fluid <i>is</i> an Exarch's sense of self and self-image?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T16:58:02-07:00","id":943114,"title":"","content":"Why would a God show himself and let the slightest opportunity for some upstart Arch-mage attempt at taking it's place though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:04:23-07:00","id":943118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=943114#post943114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a God show himself and let the slightest opportunity for some upstart Arch-mage attempt at taking it's place though?</div> </div> </div> </div>...because it says, canonically, that Ministers report directly to the Exarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:10:01-07:00","id":943126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=943118#post943118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...because it says, canonically, that Ministers report directly to the Exarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be the way you're wording it but I don't believe meeting face to face is strictly necessary for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:11:26-07:00","id":943130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=943126#post943126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It may be the way you're wording it but I don't believe meeting face to face is strictly necessary for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>How so?<br /> <br /> (By the way, I apologize if I sounded snippy. Not my intent!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:20:05-07:00","id":943138,"title":"","content":"Well, for instance, don't they have a huge gaping portal in their souls leading directly to their master's astral domain? Can't they, I don't know, possess the dude at will, let alone communicate with him anywhere, anytime like the proverbial shoulder imp?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:23:45-07:00","id":943140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=943138#post943138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, for instance, don't they have a huge gaping portal in their souls leading directly to their master's astral domain? Can't they, I don't know, possess the dude at will, let alone communicate with him anywhere, anytime like the proverbial shoulder imp?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of that! It makes sense. The Seers believe the Exarchs may well have entire universes inside themselves, so maybe 'face-to-face' is better described as 'face-to-tiny-fragment-of-almighty-worldmonster'!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:27:58-07:00","id":943145,"title":"","content":"I don't think the Exarchs are meant to be ever encountered, not even as an Archmaster. Their Ochema, sure. But IM even mentions that when visiting their Exarchiates (or whatever their Supernal palaces are called) the places appear to be empty. <br /> <br /> This is one of those things that, if it has an answer, it will be different from one chronicle to another, and should never be canonical. If you really want them to appear in your story, then that's awesome but you probably have to make them up yourself. Pebbles gives a good example of how it could be done. However there are lots of potential plot twists that a meeting with an Exarch could lead to besides you simply finding one. From them never existing, to actually NOT being in the Supernal (Exarch means to rule from outside, people assume it means they rule the Fallen from the Supernal, but Archmasters know both are more like the two sides of a coin than one world within another, maybe Exarchs are now literally outside...) to there being something even more sinister occupying their thrones or maybe they are simply the whole realm (which is a very common tendency in CoD gamelines, the more powerful you are, the more you become a place rather than a discrete being).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T17:34:08-07:00","id":943152,"title":"","content":"I love a unified CofD cosmology, but I prefer the Exarchs literally being in the Supernal World. The whole 'old gods are overthrown by new gods' vibe would be lost, I think, if the Exarchs weren't really there (or even in existence).<br /> <br /> However...the idea the Exarchs have transcended perceptible reality, even on a Supernal scale, is pretty frickin' <i>awesome</i>!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:16:43-07:00","id":943195,"title":"","content":"Nothing about the cosmology would be unified by the presence of the Exarchs in or out of the Supernal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T18:36:08-07:00","id":943219,"title":"","content":"I didn't say the Exarchs unified it.<br /> <br /> To explain: one thing that irked the s**t out of me with the oWoD was the jagged, ill-fitting 'cosmology'. This, in my opinion, is one of many features the CofD got more-or-less right. I'll admit, it's not a perfect fit, but things mesh <i>much</i> better.<br /> <br /> So, by 'unified cosmology', in this instance I'm referring to 'the cosmology' as written, with the edges smoothed over by me as a Storyteller. Having the Exarchs genuinely in charge of the Supernal World is 'a better fit'.<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe I'm rambling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T20:07:33-07:00","id":943326,"title":"","content":"I don't even remember where I saw it, I think it was in some long-forgotten Actual Play, but my favorite depiction of the Exarchs is just a gigantic, middle-aged, butt naked human being that's visibly and obviously completely out of place in the Supernal Realms. You'd only get glimpses of their elbow or earlobe or kneecap, they're always obscured by clouds or conveniently placed objects or weird camera angles. They speak in loud, booming voices but stutter and second-guess themselves and double back on their words and generally sound like you're distracting them from a very important phone call. Think Wizard of Oz, man behind the curtain, on a cosmic scale. Nothing about them says &quot;these are the right beings to be in charge of reality.&quot; An audience with an Exarch shouldn't be <i>funny</i> exactly, but awkward, uncomfortable, underwhelming, vaguely pathetic.<br /> <br /> It's really, really important to me that the Exarchs are just a bunch of assholes, just like you, who by complete chance happened to be the first ones up the Ladder before they kicked it down. There's nothing majestic or awe-inspiring about them in the flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:50:18-07:00","id":945846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=943326#post943326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even remember where I saw it, I think it was in some long-forgotten Actual Play, but my favorite depiction of the Exarchs is just a gigantic, middle-aged, butt naked human being that's visibly and obviously completely out of place in the Supernal Realms. You'd only get glimpses of their elbow or earlobe or kneecap, they're always obscured by clouds or conveniently placed objects or weird camera angles. They speak in loud, booming voices but stutter and second-guess themselves and double back on their words and generally sound like you're distracting them from a very important phone call. Think Wizard of Oz, man behind the curtain, on a cosmic scale. Nothing about them says &amp;quot;these are the right beings to be in charge of reality.&amp;quot; An audience with an Exarch shouldn't be <i>funny</i> exactly, but awkward, uncomfortable, underwhelming, vaguely pathetic.<br /> <br /> It's really, really important to me that the Exarchs are just a bunch of assholes, just like you, who by complete chance happened to be the first ones up the Ladder before they kicked it down. There's nothing majestic or awe-inspiring about them in the flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div>This...is <i>awesome</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T16:32:38-07:00","id":946545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=943326#post943326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't even remember where I saw it, I think it was in some long-forgotten Actual Play, but my favorite depiction of the Exarchs is just a gigantic, middle-aged, butt naked human being that's visibly and obviously completely out of place in the Supernal Realms. You'd only get glimpses of their elbow or earlobe or kneecap, they're always obscured by clouds or conveniently placed objects or weird camera angles. They speak in loud, booming voices but stutter and second-guess themselves and double back on their words and generally sound like you're distracting them from a very important phone call. Think Wizard of Oz, man behind the curtain, on a cosmic scale. Nothing about them says &quot;these are the right beings to be in charge of reality.&quot; An audience with an Exarch shouldn't be <i>funny</i> exactly, but awkward, uncomfortable, underwhelming, vaguely pathetic.<br /> <br /> It's really, really important to me that the Exarchs are just a bunch of assholes, just like you, who by complete chance happened to be the first ones up the Ladder before they kicked it down. There's nothing majestic or awe-inspiring about them in the flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's definitely an interesting way to get that particular theme across, and I love it.<br /> <br /> However, as to the more specific question about Ministers seeing their Exarchs and reporting directly to them, recall that it says they report directly. However, that doesn't necessarily mean direct communion face-to-face. It could be they speak through scrying portals, but never see more than the Exarch's seal. It could be they commune through the aforementioned hole-in-a-soul, and it's a voice they hear. It could be that they get text messages on a Supernal Cellphone in their head. They're still contacting them directly, but don't ever have to see the Exarch.<br /> <br /> Moses once got to see God, at his request as a favor; the Lord allowed this, but only allowed the prophet to see His back, for to see His face would kill any mortal, even a prophet, and thus God blocked the cave Moses was in with His hand as He passed. Moses was speaking directly to God, and saw His manifestations (a cloud, the burning bush, and a voice that spoke to him), but never got to see God head on. At the very least, even if their true presence is not so destructive, it seems to me that the Exarchs would take inspiration from this, and never actually allow even their Ministers on the Fallen World to see their true form. They would hide it behind symbols and masks and speak with magically amplified booming voices; they would appear (if they chose to do so in their communions with the Ministers) as clouds or avatars. They would appear majestic, if they chose to make themselves visible in the mortal plane.<br /> <br /> But it would never be their true form. It would always be another layer of symbols to hide the truth of their existence, and to make them feel divine. The Ministers still commune with them directly, but it is not face-to-face, unadulterated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:38:12-07:00","id":946573,"title":"","content":"I think my take on the Exarchs is the opposite of where this thread has gone: Of course the Exarchs are majestic, incredible symbols, fractal depictions of misery and tyranny that can only be described even slightly by the intricate iron seals they present. Not because the Exarchs themselves were, in life, necessarily the most majestic and powerful (though, even if they were once human, they were the humans who thought to become the symbols of tyranny, even if they came to power with the Star Ladder). They are that way because it is the nature of the Supernal to imbue things with meaning, and anything which exists within the Supernal is either torn apart on a semiotic level or deified. Ascended mages become a living symbol, and other mages can use their symbolism as yantras, and the Exarchs are that to the umpteenth power. No matter what they once were, the Exarchs are nothing human now. They are also loathsome - every element of their symbolism declares 'you will kneel, worm' and they embody monstrous abuses of power to maintain their hold.<br /> In short - the Exarchs are entire symbolic languages of degradation and cruel strength, and to downplay them seems to me to miss the point. They did win. They did become the new gods, the rulers of the world. They are, in fact, divine now. And they shouldn't be, at all, because they are petty and vicious and horrible, no matter how majestic their symbolism.<br /> <br /> Edit to clarify: Basically, I think the Exarchs should in fact be terrible and beautiful to behold, because throughout history tyrants and tyranny have had a majesty, poetry written in their honor, the works. And that doesn't mean their tyranny or power is more acceptable, at all. The Exarchs are gods - but they're monstrous gods. Plenty of Bound should be similarly numinous-and-awful, in less human ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3547,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","user":"SonOfSilkAndStone","date":". 08-08-2016, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T17:44:06-07:00","id":946578,"title":"","content":"Well, considering that characters are actually the avatars of beings outside their world, I think a fair illustration could be a <i>mirror</i>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:19:28-07:00","id":946601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SonOfSilkAndStone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=946573#post946573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter what they once were, the Exarchs are nothing human now. They are also loathsome - every element of their symbolism declares 'you will kneel, worm' and they embody monstrous abuses of power to maintain their hold.<br /> In short - the Exarchs are entire symbolic languages of degradation and cruel strength, and to downplay them seems to me to miss the point. They did win. They did become the new gods, the rulers of the world. They are, in fact, divine now. And they shouldn't be, at all, because they are petty and vicious and horrible, no matter how majestic their symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess my view as an ST is: that's so <i>obvious</i>, though. Of course the players (and their characters) are going to expect the Exarchs to be the supreme ultimate final boss overlord monster, cloaked in glory and power. But when you really want to make an encounter memorable, I think it's better to go sideways than straight up, so to speak. Showing the Exarchs as painfully human, in sharp contrast to how the Ministries imagine and depict the Iron Seals in their iconography, reinforces that the whole <i>system </i>is wrong. When the players are expecting something of world-shaking power, absurd can be scarier than majestic.<br /> <br /> You know what would be a great model for an Exarch? Boss Smiley in the Teen President issue of Sandman: <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/kuRam08.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.imgur.com/kuRam08.jpg</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T22:18:25-07:00","id":946745,"title":"","content":"I disagree that always undercutting is a great move. It can serve to undercut the players' enthusiasm as well. Sometimes, a story needs to be the standard structure, performed as well as possible.<br /> I wouldn't, personally, ever have the Exarchs appear to mages except in the shapes of their palaces and their actions in the world. They have no need of embodiment.<br /> But if the players managed to get to the point of meeting the Exarchs - Ascending, or some massive plot-ending event - I would give them something dramatic and ennobling, because there's nowhere for the story to go after the Exarchs anyways. Why give them a story that peters off into a bad joke, rather than having a conclusion?<br /> Boss Smiley, for the record, isn't particularly absurd in context. He's grotesque because he is, in fact, the symbol underlying everything in the story. The story is, after all, already absurd, and it turns out that the God of the story is the monster, the devil who tempted the savior-figure. I'd argue it's more in line with my read on the Exarchs than the bathos version. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3547-sonofsilkandstone","name":"SonOfSilkAndStone","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:11:26-07:00","id":947842,"title":"","content":"The Unity looks like a trillion people, who all look like you.<br /> <br /> The General looks divided or in conflict with Themselves.<br /> <br /> The Father looks like Caladriu's perspective, because while I view the other Exarchs differently I can't help but find that one fits the Father damned well.<br /> <br /> The Eye is looking at you, you see yourself and everything else from Its perspective.<br /> <br /> The Chancellor looks objectively and utterly beautiful.<br /> <br /> The Prophet looks like the person you idolise the most, but -wrong-.<br /> <br /> The Ruin looks like the inevitable end of everything you hold dear.<br /> <br /> The Psychopomp looks like the rot that eats away at the Universe.<br /> <br /> The Nemesis looks like the shadow of all things.<br /> <br /> The Raptor looks like a whole Universe of flesh and frenzy, constantly growing even as it devours itself endlessly.<br /> <br /> The Gate looks like absolutely nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T10:20:13-07:00","id":947848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=947842#post947842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unity looks like a trillion people, who all look like you.<br /> <br /> The General looks divided or in conflict with Themselves.<br /> <br /> The Father looks like Caladriu's perspective, because while I view the other Exarchs differently I can't help but find that one fits the Father damned well.<br /> <br /> The Eye is looking at you, you see yourself and everything else from Its perspective.<br /> <br /> The Chancellor looks objectively and utterly beautiful.<br /> <br /> The Prophet looks like the person you idolise the most, but -wrong-.<br /> <br /> The Ruin looks like the inevitable end of everything you hold dear.<br /> <br /> The Psychopomp looks like the rot that eats away at the Universe.<br /> <br /> The Nemesis looks like the shadow of all things.<br /> <br /> The Raptor looks like a whole Universe of flesh and frenzy, constantly growing even as it devours itself endlessly.<br /> <br /> The Gate looks like absolutely nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T12:53:49-07:00","id":947967,"title":"","content":"I'm not going to be able to top Kleptomania, but just to mention: I once ran a weird gonzo offbeat Seers of the Throne game on roll20 which prominently featured the Secret Order of the Gate in the background, and whenever the Eleventh Seal was influencing a scene, we'd thematically suggest its influence with Weird Tweets and glitch gifs overwriting local adverts and TV broadcasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Seinfeld S11E05 &quot;The Gate&quot;</b><br /> GEORGE: I wanna invoke it, Jerry! It's callin' me in my dreams! This is my ticket to the big time!<br /> JERRY: You heard what the Tetrarch said, George! You can't worship the Gate, it's the Gate!<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://usvsth3m.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/tumblr_mkxr1uirZZ1rwd0doo1_400.gif\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.mirror.co.uk/nav-web-static/main-ed1c6c6a14f311118becc01b2f3ea96a5f95956e/public/assets/mirror/logos/logo-mirror-social-sharing.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://usvsth3m.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/tumblr_mkxr1uirZZ1rwd0doo1_400.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> Us vs Th3m: Bored? We have games, quizzes, \u270d &amp; LOLs \u27a0 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://usvsth3m.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/tumblr_mkxr1uirZZ1rwd0doo1_400.gif\" target=\"_blank\"> http://usvsth3m.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/tumblr_mkxr1uirZZ1rwd0doo1_400.gif </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Alleviate your boredom with our web games, quizzes, LOLs &amp; strong opinions. Distractions and debate to make you (\u2742\u203f\u2742), {\u0ca0_\u0ca0} or &macr;_(\u30c4)_/&macr; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T18:22:34-07:00","id":948221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=947967#post947967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not going to be able to top Kleptomania, but just to mention: I once ran a weird gonzo offbeat Seers of the Throne game on roll20 which prominently featured the Secret Order of the Gate in the background, and whenever the Eleventh Seal was influencing a scene, we'd thematically suggest its influence with Weird Tweets and glitch gifs overwriting local adverts and TV broadcasts.<br /> <br /> <b>Seinfeld S11E05 &quot;The Gate&quot;</b><br /> GEORGE: I wanna invoke it, Jerry! It's callin' me in my dreams! This is my ticket to the big time!<br /> JERRY: You heard what the Tetrarch said, George! You can't worship the Gate, it's the Gate!<br /> <a href=\"http://usvsth3m.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/tumblr_mkxr1uirZZ1rwd0doo1_400.gif\" target=\"_blank\">http://usvsth3m.com/wp-content/uploa...d0doo1_400.gif</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I really want to watch that Seinfeld episode now.<br /> I would totally worship the Gate if it gave me access to its weird media manipulations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 08-10-2016, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T01:08:55-07:00","id":948435,"title":"","content":"<b>We know Ministers <i>could </i>see Exarchs - but how Prelates communicate with them?</b> I have Prelate of Eye in my game and still I do not know how to convey what she is experiencing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T02:01:35-07:00","id":948454,"title":"","content":"Were you not paying attention to the others who posted ways that Exarchs communicate with their subordinates? Dreams, visions, the static on their favorite radio station, they can do it pretty much any way they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T13:52:28-07:00","id":953412,"title":"","content":"Each Exarch is a colossus; a monstrous, misshapen effigy of a human form, assembled out of the symbols that define each of the Iron Seals. The General's flesh is blood-soaked earth, scarified with trenches and barbed wire; its fingers are tank barrels, and its eyes atomic detonations. The Father's face is made of a thousand smaller faces: masks and idols and effigies of every god in whose name humankind has shed blood. Its breath is a wind of sickly-sweet incense, barely hiding the scent of burning flesh. The Raptor is made from a million lesser beasts sewn together -- some living, screaming, tearing at themselves and each other; others dead and decaying, with grotesque flora and fungi sprouting from their bodies.<br /> <br /> Barely visible at the heart of each titan is a withered, atrophied, impossibly aged human body -- the last remnant of the human mage it once was. So wizened are these husks that it is impossible discern face, race, or even gender. In any case, the Exarchs themselves have long forgotten who they once were, or what passions drove them to usurp godhood. Nothing remains of them but the joy of having power (and they <i>are</i> joyous) and the fear of losing it (and they <i>are</i> fearful.) Most of the time, they don't even remember what they've lost, let alone regret it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/40-dspaul","name":"DSPaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T05:33:37-07:00","id":953760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DSPaul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/943078-the-visage-of-an-exarch?p=953412#post953412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each Exarch is a colossus; a monstrous, misshapen effigy of a human form, assembled out of the symbols that define each of the Iron Seals. The General's flesh is blood-soaked earth, scarified with trenches and barbed wire; its fingers are tank barrels, and its eyes atomic detonations. The Father's face is made of a thousand smaller faces: masks and idols and effigies of every god in whose name humankind has shed blood. Its breath is a wind of sickly-sweet incense, barely hiding the scent of burning flesh. The Raptor is made from a million lesser beasts sewn together -- some living, screaming, tearing at themselves and each other; others dead and decaying, with grotesque flora and fungi sprouting from their bodies.<br /> <br /> Barely visible at the heart of each titan is a withered, atrophied, impossibly aged human body -- the last remnant of the human mage it once was. So wizened are these husks that it is impossible discern face, race, or even gender. In any case, the Exarchs themselves have long forgotten who they once were, or what passions drove them to usurp godhood. Nothing remains of them but the joy of having power (and they <i>are</i> joyous) and the fear of losing it (and they <i>are</i> fearful.) Most of the time, they don't even remember what they've lost, let alone regret it.</div> </div> </div> </div>...you win!<br /> <br /> I am <i>totally</i> using this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}